Selection sort intuition:
	Pluck the smallest available number and drop it in the index closest to 0.
	Smallest number goes in 0, 2nd smallest number goes in index 1, etc
	
	
Array: 4 3 2 1


1st pass: 1

1 3 2 4

1 2 3 4

1 2 3 4

On average, the inner loop runs for n/2
Total performance 0(n) * 0(n/2) = 0(n^2)
	
Code:
public static void selectionSort(int[] arr) {
	for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; ++i) {
		int minIndex = i;
		for (int j = i+1; j < arr.length; ++j) {
			if (arr[j] < arr[minIndex]) {
				minIndex = j;
			}
		}
		int temp = arr[i];
		arr[i] = arr[minIndex];
		arr[minIndex] = temp;
	}
}

